  "Question": "If \\(\\dfrac mn=\\dfrac43\\) and \\(\\dfrac rt=\\dfrac9{14},\\) the value of \\(\\dfrac{3mr-nt}{4nt-7mr}\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-5\\dfrac12\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac{11}{14}\\)",
    "C": "\\(-1\\dfrac14\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{11}{14}\\)",
    "E": "\\(-\\dfrac23\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Both parts of the expression involve only \\(mr\\) and \\(nt\\), so first find their ratio. The given fractions require \\(n\\ne0\\) and \\(t\\ne0\\), and\n\\[\n\\frac{mr}{nt}=\\frac mn\\cdot\\frac rt\n=\\frac43\\cdot\\frac9{14}=\\frac67.\n\\]\nConsequently, \\(4nt-7mr=(4-6)nt=-2nt\\ne0\\), so the requested expression is defined. Dividing its numerator and denominator by \\(nt\\) gives\n\\[\n\\frac{3mr-nt}{4nt-7mr}\n=\\frac{3\\left(\\frac67\\right)-1}{4-7\\left(\\frac67\\right)}\n=\\frac{11/7}{-2}\n=-\\frac{11}{14}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{-\\frac{11}{14}}\\), choice B.",
